  "notes": "Measured on the A321neo (B-32CY, left side); the 737 and 787 carry the same layout. The belly from directly below isn't checked beyond the 737's oblique view. The wing undersides carry '厦门航空' (not drawn). Colors by eye. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the 737-800, Xiamen's commonest type (B-5632, left, 2025-03-21; measured between its doors and by the window line): the titles had been measured on the A321neo, whose longer body made their shares too small; now the Chinese runs x 0.219-0.306, XIAMEN 0.309-0.407, AIR 0.408-0.443, on the 737. On the right side (B-1117) the line reads XIAMEN AIR from the tail with AIR next to the Chinese, so XIAMEN and AIR get a pair per side; the Chinese there reads from the nose toward the tail (right to left as seen), which the title can't express: it is drawn reading normally. The belly bands' edges are curves (smooth).",
  "history": "New entry (not in Skyarium v1): Xiamen Airlines flies under its own ICAO code (CXA) and its own egret brand, though China Southern owns a majority of it."
